cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Surface protein targets in cancer: a reproducible pipeline for
  identifying cell-surface proteins over-expressed in tumours and
  absent from healthy tissue
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ingrid-per
repository-code: https://github.com/ingrid-per/surfaceome_atlas_challenge
url: https://ingrid-per.github.io/surfaceome_atlas_challenge/
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that narrows the 20,431 reviewed human proteins to ten candidate
  cell-surface cancer targets, by combining curated and predicted membrane
  topology (UniProt and DeepTMHMM, with a separate route for GPI-anchored
  proteins), differential expression between TCGA tumours and GTEx healthy
  tissue reprocessed through a single pipeline, and a specificity score against
  the highest-expressing healthy tissue across two independent atlases. The
  selection rule is recorded before the ranking is produced, and the whole
  selection is re-run under 270 threshold combinations to report how much each
  candidate depends on the thresholds chosen.
keywords:
  - cancer
  - surfaceome
  - target discovery
  - transcriptomics
  - TCGA
  - GTEx
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
